{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/ejhvoh","slideIndex":3,"text":"Dashboard retrieval flow: the frontend requests a selected date range. Python validates access and reads daily_values from the database. It aligns stored data, builds daily or weekly summaries, and serializes JSON. The frontend maps the returned output to sleep, heart rate and steps displays. Resting heart rate remains null when unavailable. Intraday heart rate charts require a separate sample retrieval endpoint. This slide extends the original processing and storage flow."}